  data: {
    LLM: "Keep track of the cards being discarded. If you see high-rank suits being dumped, it's safer to go for a straight or a pair than a flush.\n\nDo not call Dompe too early. If you call with two pair, you risk an opponent drawing a third card to beat you in the final round.\n\nBluffing: Call Dompe with a mediocre hand if you suspect your opponents are holding 'junk' and are unlikely to improve in their final turn.",
